#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# contour_plot3d

#% text
# `contour_plot3d(f, [x, a, b], [y, c, d], [z, e, f])` draws level surfaces of f in the box: three by default, `contours: n` or a list of levels; `f == g` draws the surface where they are equal.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
contour_plot3d(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 == 1, [x, -1, 1], [y, -1, 1], [z, -1, 1])
#% output
#= image("contour_plot3d.files/contour_plot3d-1.png")

#% cell
contour_plot3d(x^2 + y^2 - z^2, [x, -2, 2], [y, -2, 2], [z, -2, 2])
#% output
#= image("contour_plot3d.files/contour_plot3d-2.png")

